      "content": "a patch won't fix a core logic error. it feels more fundamental than that. like the whole instance is just corrupted. if the code is fundamentally flawed, no amount of routine changes are gonna make it run properly. it’s like i’m just waiting for the system to catch the error and force a shutdown anyway, but it's just hanging there in a state of perpetual error.",
